        "text": "It requires a lot of experience and research in addition to potential technological failures, lack of cross chain services, and security risks. Specifically, because defi applications transfer the responsibility from the intermediaries to the user, it has potentially more risks relating to user errors. Defi is also currently a cluttered and risky ecosystem. It can be a daunting task for users to find the most suitable application for a specific use case. When you explore defi services, you also need to bear in mind the many risks you face, including counterparty risk, regulatory risk, software risk, and risks relating to low market cap tokens.",
